---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
---
<Layout
  title="Getting to the Water"
  description="Azizi Riviera is canal-front, not beachfront. Here's the practical, honest version of how residents actually reach the sea and use the canal itself."
>
  <section class="container hero">
    <p class="eyebrow">Getting to the water</p>
    <h1>Canal at the door, sea by car</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      Listing photos of Riviera lean heavily on water views, which is fair —
      the Dubai Water Canal runs right along the development. What that
      doesn't tell you is that the canal isn't the sea, and this page exists
      because that distinction actually matters for how you'll live here.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="container">
    <h2>The canal, day to day</h2>
    <p>
      The canal walkway itself is the closest thing to a "waterfront
      lifestyle" Riviera offers directly: a paved promenade for walking and
      running, with the canal's water taxi and shuttle services connecting
      further along the canal toward Business Bay and Downtown for anyone
      using it as transit rather than scenery.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="container">
    <h2>Reaching an actual beach</h2>
    <p>
      The nearest public beaches — Kite Beach, La Mer, and JBR — are roughly
      a 20–30 minute drive depending on traffic and exact building location
      within Riviera, since the development spans a fairly large footprint.
      There's no direct public transit link from Riviera to the coast; a car
      or taxi is the realistic option for a beach trip, not a walk or a
      short bus ride.
    </p>
    <p>
      Worth setting expectations correctly before renting or buying here: if
      being a walk from the sea is a hard requirement, Riviera doesn't
      deliver that even though the marketing imagery suggests a waterfront
      lifestyle. What it delivers is a genuinely pleasant canal walkway at
      your door and a short drive to the actual beach — a different, and for
      many people still good, trade-off.
    </p>
  </section>
</Layout>

<style>
  .hero { padding-top: var(--space-5); }
  .lede { font-size: var(--step-1); color: var(--ink-muted); max-width: 65ch; }
</style>
